/*  Maps — `TypeChecker.Maps.cs`: what may be a key, a map written out, looked in, written to and
    walked through — and `Exit`, from `TypeChecker.Failures.cs`, for being as small.

    ★ A key is a scalar, or a record of scalars: something compared by what it holds and unable to
    change underneath the map.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    /// `IsValidMapKeyType`: a scalar, a record of keys, or a voidable or closed union of them.
    Bind fact to is-valid-key, given (the node shape):
        Define kind as shape's kind.
        If kind is "NumberType" or kind is "TextType" or kind is "FactType" or kind is "BitsType", return true.
        If kind is "VoidableType", return cast is-valid-key on (cast field-of on (shape, 1)).
        If kind is "RecordType":
            For each positional in (cast field-of on (shape, 1))'s children, repeat:
                If cast is-valid-key on (positional) is false, return false.
            Done.
            For each pair in (cast field-of on (shape, 2))'s children, repeat:
                If cast is-valid-key on (item 2 of pair's children) is false, return false.
            Done.
            Return true.
        Done.
        If kind is "UnionType":
            Define cases as cast field-of on (shape, 1).
            If cases's kind is not "list", return false.
            For each one-case in cases's children, repeat:
                If cast is-valid-key on (one-case) is false, return false.
            Done.
            Return true.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    Bind text to ordinal-word, given (the number place):
        Define words as a series with ("first", "second", "third", "fourth", "fifth", "sixth", "seventh", "eighth", "ninth").
        If place is less than 10, return item place of words.
        Return "{place}th".
    Done.

    /// `RequireValidMapKeyType`.
    Bind void or failure to require-map-key, given (the node key-type, the number at-row):
        If cast is-valid-key on (key-type), return.
        If cast beyond-types on (key-type), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("a key that is a {key-type's kind}")).
        Define spoken as cast type-words on (key-type).
        // A record is refused for what is INSIDE it, so the message names that part.
        If key-type's kind is "RecordType":
            Define bad-name as "a field".
            Define bad-type as key-type.
            Define place as 0.
            For each positional in (cast field-of on (key-type, 1))'s children, repeat:
                Increment place by 1.
                If bad-name is "a field" and cast is-valid-key on (positional) is false:
                    The bad-name becomes "the {cast ordinal-word on (place)} field".
                    The bad-type becomes positional.
                Done.
            Done.
            For each pair in (cast field-of on (key-type, 2))'s children, repeat:
                If bad-name is "a field" and cast is-valid-key on (item 2 of pair's children) is false:
                    The bad-name becomes "'{cast unquoted on (item 1 of pair's children)}'".
                    The bad-type becomes item 2 of pair's children.
                Done.
            Done.
            Define held as cast type-words on (bad-type).
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("a key has to be a scalar or a record of scalars, and this record holds {held}",
                "a {held} can be changed after it is used as a key, and then the entry it was stored under could never be found again",
                at-row, "use '{spoken}' as a map key",
                "Leave {bad-name} out of the key — a record of numbers, text, facts or bit patterns is fine, and those are what can be compared and cannot change underneath the map.")).
        Done.
        Define kind as key-type's kind.
        Define why as "only a scalar, or a record of scalars, can be compared as a key".
        If kind is "SeriesType" or kind is "MapType" or kind is "MatrixType":
            The why becomes "it can be changed after it is used as a key, and then the entry it was stored under could never be found again".
        Done.
        If kind is "ObjectType":
            The why becomes "an object's fields can be written after it is used as a key, and then the entry it was stored under could never be found again".
        Done.
        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{spoken}' can't be a map key", why, at-row,
            "use a '{spoken}' as a map key",
            "A key is a number, text, a fact, a bit pattern, or a record of those. Key by a field that is one of them — a name, an id — or by a record of them, like a (row, column) pair.")).
    Done.

    Bind node to map-type-of, given (the node key-type, the node value-type):
        Define shape as cast plain-type on ("MapType").
        Cast shape's add on (key-type).
        Cast shape's add on (value-type).
        Return shape.
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to infer-map-literal unto checker, given (the node said):
        Define key-written as cast field-of on (said, 1).
        Define value-written as cast field-of on (said, 2).
        Define pairs as (cast field-of on (said, 3))'s children.
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (said, 4)).
        If the number of pairs is 0:
            Cast require-map-key on (key-written, at-row) or pass the failure off.
            Define empty-map as cast map-type-of on (key-written, value-written).
            Cast one's check-resolves on (empty-map) or pass the failure off.
            Return empty-map.
        Done.
        If cast is-nothing on (key-written) is false and cast is-nothing on (value-written) is false:
            Cast require-map-key on (key-written, at-row) or pass the failure off.
            If cast beyond-types on (value-written), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("a map of {value-written's kind}")).
            For each pair in pairs, repeat:
                Define key-type as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (pair, 1)) or pass the failure off.
                If cast is-none on (key-type) is false and cast assignable on (key-written, key-type) is false:
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("this atlas uses {cast type-words on (key-written)} keys", "",
                        at-row, "use a {cast type-words on (key-type)} as a key",
                        "Keys in this atlas must be {cast plural-words on (key-written)}.")).
                Done.
                Define value-type as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (pair, 2)) or pass the failure off.
                If cast is-none on (value-type) is false and cast assignable on (value-written, value-type) is false:
                    If cast beyond-types on (value-type), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("a {value-type's kind} in a map")).
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("this atlas holds {cast plural-words on (value-written)}", "",
                        at-row, "store a {cast type-words on (value-type)} in it",
                        "Values in this atlas must be {cast plural-words on (value-written)}.")).
                Done.
            Done.
            Define written-map as cast map-type-of on (key-written, value-written).
            Cast one's check-resolves on (written-map) or pass the failure off.
            Return written-map.
        Done.

        Define inferred-key as cast unknown-type.
        Define inferred-value as cast unknown-type.
        For each pair in pairs, repeat:
            Define key-type as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (pair, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            Define value-type as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (pair, 2)) or pass the failure off.
            If cast is-none on (key-type) is false:
                If cast is-none on (inferred-key):
                    Cast require-map-key on (key-type, at-row) or pass the failure off.
                    The inferred-key becomes key-type.
                Done.
                Otherwise if cast same-type on (inferred-key, key-type) is false:
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("all keys in a map must be the same type",
                        "The first key is a {cast type-words on (inferred-key)}, so all keys must be {cast plural-words on (inferred-key)}",
                        at-row, "mix a {cast type-words on (key-type)} key with {cast type-words on (inferred-key)} keys",
                        "Make all keys the same type.")).
                Done.
            Done.
            If cast is-none on (value-type) is false:
                If cast is-none on (inferred-value):
                    The inferred-value becomes value-type.
                Done.
                Otherwise if cast same-type on (inferred-value, value-type) is false:
                    If cast beyond-types on (value-type) or cast beyond-types on (inferred-value):
                        Return a failure (cast not-judged on ("a map of mixed kinds")).
                    Done.
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("all values in a map must be the same type",
                        "The first value is a {cast type-words on (inferred-value)}, so all values must be {cast plural-words on (inferred-value)}",
                        at-row, "mix a {cast type-words on (value-type)} value with {cast type-words on (inferred-value)} values",
                        "Make all values the same type.")).
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        If cast is-none on (inferred-key) or cast is-none on (inferred-value), return cast unknown-type.
        Return cast map-type-of on (inferred-key, inferred-value).
    Done.

    /// A key where a map's key goes — `this map uses <K> keys` in the words each site gives.
    Bind void or failure to check-map-key unto checker, given (the node map-shape, the node key-said,
            the number at-row, the text action):
        Define key-type as cast one's infer on (key-said) or pass the failure off.
        Define wanted as cast field-of on (map-shape, 1).
        If cast is-none on (key-type) is false and cast assignable on (wanted, key-type) is false:
            If cast beyond-types on (key-type) or cast beyond-types on (wanted), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("a key of another kind")).
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("this map uses {cast type-words on (wanted)} keys", "",
                at-row, "{action} a {cast type-words on (key-type)} key",
                "Keys in this map are {cast plural-words on (wanted)}.")).
        Done.
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to infer-map-lookup unto checker, given (the node said):
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (said, 3)).
        Define map-shape as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (said, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-none on (map-shape), return map-shape.
        If map-shape's kind is not "MapType":
            If cast beyond-types on (map-shape), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("an entry of a {map-shape's kind}")).
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'the entry for ... in ...' requires a map", "",
                at-row, "look up an entry in a {cast type-words on (map-shape)}",
                "Only maps support entry lookup. Use 'the entry for key in map'.")).
        Done.
        Cast one's check-map-key on (map-shape, cast field-of on (said, 2), at-row, "look up using") or pass the failure off.
        Define held as cast field-of on (map-shape, 2).
        If held's kind is "VoidableType", return held.
        Return cast wrapped on ("VoidableType", held).
    Done.

    /// `has a key for` and `has an entry for` — a fact, whatever it is asked of.
    Bind node or failure to infer-map-has unto checker, given (the node said):
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (said, 3)).
        Define map-shape as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (said, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        If map-shape's kind is "MapType":
            Cast one's check-map-key on (map-shape, cast field-of on (said, 2), at-row, "check for") or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Return cast plain-type on ("FactType").
    Done.

    Bind void or failure to check-map-set unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define target as cast field-of on (statement, 1).
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 4)).
        Define map-shape as cast one's infer on (target) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-none on (map-shape), return.
        If map-shape's kind is not "MapType":
            If cast beyond-types on (map-shape), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("an entry of a {map-shape's kind}")).
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("the target of a map entry assignment must be a map", "",
                at-row, "assign a map entry on a non-map value",
                "Only maps support 'in map, the entry for key becomes value'.")).
        Done.
        Define key-type as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Define wanted-key as cast field-of on (map-shape, 1).
        If cast is-none on (key-type) is false and cast assignable on (wanted-key, key-type) is false:
            If cast beyond-types on (key-type), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("a key of another kind")).
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("this map uses {cast type-words on (wanted-key)} keys", "",
                at-row, "use a {cast type-words on (key-type)} as a key",
                "Keys in this map must be {cast plural-words on (wanted-key)}.")).
        Done.
        Define value as cast field-of on (statement, 3).
        Define value-type as cast one's infer on (value) or pass the failure off.
        Define wanted-value as cast field-of on (map-shape, 2).
        If cast is-none on (value-type) is false and cast assignable on (wanted-value, value-type) is false:
            If cast beyond-types on (value-type) or cast beyond-types on (wanted-value), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("a value of another kind")).
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("this map holds {cast plural-words on (wanted-value)}", "",
                at-row, "store a {cast type-words on (value-type)} in it",
                "Values in this map must be {cast plural-words on (wanted-value)}.")).
        Done.
        Cast one's check-region-store on (value, value-type, cast one's container-depth on (target), at-row,
            "store a region-scoped value in a map that lives in a longer-lived region") or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    /// `Exit.` and `Exit with <status>.` — a whole number from 0 to 255 when it is written out.
    Bind void or failure to check-exit unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define status as cast field-of on (statement, 1).
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)).
        If cast is-nothing on (status), return.
        Define status-type as cast one's infer on (status) or pass the failure off.
        If status-type's kind is not "NumberType":
            Define spoken as "void".
            If cast is-none on (status-type) is false, the spoken becomes cast type-words on (status-type).
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("an exit status must be a number, not {spoken}", "",
                at-row, "exit with something that is not a number", "Write 'Exit with 1.' — a whole number from 0 to 255.")).
        Done.
        If status's kind is not "NumberLiteral", return.
        Define written as (cast field-of on (status, 1))'s word.
        Define amount as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (status, 1)).
        If amount % 1 is not 0:
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("{written} is not an exit status — a status is a whole number", "",
                at-row, "exit with a status that is not whole", "Statuses run from 0 to 255 with nothing in between.")).
        Done.
        If amount is less than 0 or amount is greater than 255:
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("{written} is not an exit status — they run from 0 to 255", "",
                at-row, "exit with a status outside 0 to 255",
                "The operating system keeps only the low eight bits, so a wider number would leave with something else entirely.")).
        Done.
    Done.
Done.
